Z||000000||SilverFieroV6||05-24-2001||10:24 PM||||The car after warm up seems to always be running right around 220.  I havent checked the thermostat.  was wondering if there is something on the thermostat tha says what temp it is?  I was thinking about going and getting a 180 or maybe a little cooler one than that, as there is a lot of traffic where i live in the summer time and frequently get stuck in it.  <BR>Thanks<BR>Sam Clark||||reg||13
Z||000001||PBJ||05-24-2001||10:50 PM||||Yes usually the temp is stamped in the theromstat, but if you are taking the time to remove it and inspect it I would just go ahead and install a new one anyways.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||05-24-2001||11:02 PM||||I don't think thats running hot at all. When I don't have the rad fan on my car runs 220 in traffic in town. Granted it runs down to 160 when Im on the highway, but its a lot more air flow. Since the thermo opens at 195, and the fan comes on at like 235, I think 220 is pretty normal. Turn your rad fan on if you want to run cooler, it will run down to about 160-170.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||05-24-2001||11:09 PM||||To turn the fan on turn on the ac||||reg||1
